Leave-one-material-out fixed-logistic diagnostic results are in metrics.json.   
Inference rejects unseen materials; this diagnostic does not support deployment 
on held-out materials.                                                          

External checks and errors                                                      

Source-workbook moment check: n=131; max absolute diameter                      
error=2.22044604925e-16 μm for1000*M1/M0. No lognormal assumption for this      
ratio.                                                                          

external_checks.csv compares all10 visually verified Table1 rows from           
NTRS20130000422, p7. It recomputes count and mass-equivalent diameters from     
rounded geometric mean and geometric SD, assuming lognormal sizes. This is      
algebraic/rounding validation; those table rows cannot be treated as independent
predictive validation or matched to exact raw run IDs.                          

failure_cases.csv contains every nested OOF error with source rows and controls.
validation.png shows predicted vs derived reference classes and measured scatter
vs airflow. The scatter plot is descriptive, not causal. No uncertainty interval
or calibrated probability is claimed. Fold SD describes variability, not a      
confidence interval.                                                            

Limits                                                                          

Only84 analyzed primary records, uneven material/condition/campaign coverage,81 
conservative validation groups.82 primary physical samples collapse to81 because
the ambiguous aged51aK02 record is conservatively connected to51K01/61K02.      
Retaining reburns reflects experimental history that controls do not fully      
capture. SAME-R source quality flags are blank/unknown. AW retains source       
numeric voltages with unresolved per-row saturation and LOD; only threshold     
exceedance is modeled. Rt/R0 does not uniquely determine actual sample          
temperature. No ambient spacecraft generalization, time-to-alarm, flame/fatality
risk, detector certification, or unseen-material prediction. Full raw instrument
calibration reconstruction was not performed; source-reduced common channel is  
used. No standalone2021 report verified; exact challenge page unavailable during
audit.                                                                          
